Subject: Enable SDL3's POSIX process backend without vfork
Origin: Filnix
Upstream-Status: Not submitted
Applies-After: patches/sdl3-fork.patch

SDL 3.4 only builds the posix_spawn process backend when libc exports
vfork. Fil-C cannot provide vfork, so SDL silently fell back to the dummy
backend and SDL_CreateProcess reported "That operation is not supported"
(the testprocess suite failed). sdl3-fork.patch already makes the backend
use fork() for background processes under Fil-C; accept Fil-C here too.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -3487,8 +3487,10 @@ int main(void)
 " HAVE_POSIX_SPAWN)
   if(NOT APPLE)
     check_symbol_exists(vfork "unistd.h" LIBC_HAS_VFORK)
+    # Fil-C has no vfork; SDL_posixprocess.c uses fork there, as on Apple.
+    check_symbol_exists(__FILC__ "stddef.h" SDL_FILC)
   endif()
-  if(HAVE_POSIX_SPAWN AND (APPLE OR LIBC_HAS_VFORK))
+  if(HAVE_POSIX_SPAWN AND (APPLE OR LIBC_HAS_VFORK OR SDL_FILC))
     sdl_glob_sources(
       "${SDL3_SOURCE_DIR}/src/process/posix/*.c"
       "${SDL3_SOURCE_DIR}/src/process/posix/*.h"
